    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="0650" n="530" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg530"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Combs to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation,<lb/>Guatemala and Honduras</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1905-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September
                                21, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 305.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report the recent
                    arrest of an American negro, Charley Macmorley, by mistake for a Jamaican
                    fugitive wanted for extradition.</p>
                <p>Prompt measures were taken in his behalf, but he was already on his way to this
                    city under guard before I had the information upon which action could be taken.
                    Immediately upon his arrival here he was released and presented with 100 pesos
                    by the British charge in behalf of the Jamaican authorities and with a small sum
                    by himself.</p>
                <p>I waived the reimbursement suggested in my note of the 19th instant to the
                    Guatemalan Government, a copy of which, with other inclosures, is hereto
                    attached, since the British authorities desired to assume the expense
                    mentioned.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Leslie Combs.</hi></signed></closer>





